    "assessment": {
      "scope": "Two original works: preserved Steinsultz2024 VOR PDF with selected evidence positions; Nilges2025 VOR public-web selected text preserved as two derived carriers, never represented as raw PDF bytes. No supplement, original empirical dataset or source-native SecMOD/AVERT load-shift run was obtained.",
      "empirical": "The measured outcome aggregates CAMPD-covered ERCOT generators. Reported wind-potential HSL, normally forecast-based, is a conditional opposite-net-load proxy. Own tenth-percentile threshold groups, not a guaranteed exact10% or arbitrary hour pair, support the source-reported screening distinctions. G1 rate comparisons and residual biases, shared CAMPD, affiliated authors and selected clusters retain their limits.",
      "model": "The paper supplies selected-basis one-coordinate ranges. The book extends the vector relation to a full signed intervention. Independent blocks and a verified common baseline response along the joint direction are sufficient routes; independence is not necessary, and an arbitrary affine joint ray does not make separately selected endpoint coefficients additive. Cost ties, one-sided derivatives and selected emissions remain qualified.",
      "case": "The versioned author input fixes10 equal work units, two1h same-node lossless windows, fixed costs/capacities/rates and no intertemporal coupling. Paired dispatch preserves15MWh and10work units. At q=5/9/10, changes are−2000/0/+500kg versus original5500kg; the q10 initial-rate extrapolation is−4000kg. Receiving-rate equality across its dispatch switch does not keep the paired rate unchanged. All values are authored assumptions or exact deductions, not paper factors or field measurements.",
      "conservation": "All earlier240 sources,864 evidence rows,897 claims and185 readings remain deeply equal to the qualified Main predecessor; two new works/sources/readings, five evidence records and twelve new claims have separate identities. All19 preceding case inputs and scientific evaluation contents were preserved; producer metadata changes belong to actual new exports.",
      "review": "Independent original-source/model assessments, direct materialization of five templates, and primary integration checks support this scope. Reader and source findings were individually corrected; the final same-response clause and bounded q10 wording received a separate bounded source reread. Primary pure catalog/research/all20-case validation passed; that is distinct from the model reviewer’s direct single-case publication replay."
